{"t":9186,"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"a4ac7f0543e9f149c","run_id":"0mwm2hr4q-bd4d1106","tool_use_id":"toolu_011EuvFnwxz8P4DgTgWQ1rjc","status":"completed","output_file":"C:\\Users\\spesce\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\a3af3560164d967d\\f5fd90b6-eb8d-4c51-9b35-ab8874aa9f05\\tasks\\a4ac7f0543e9f149c.output","summary":"The sextant emerged in the early 1730s, when John Hadley in England and Thomas Godfrey in Philadelphia independently devised an instrument for measuring the angle between a celestial body and the horizon. It improved on earlier tools such as the cross-staff and the backstaff, which required the navigator to look directly at the Sun, a painful and imprecise practice. The sextant's key innovation was a pair of mirrors, an index mirror that moved with the arm and a partly silvered horizon mirror, which let the navigator superimpose the image of a body onto the horizon. Its arc spans only a sixth of a circle, yet double reflection allows angles up to 120 degrees to be read, and the arc's reach is what gave the instrument its name.\n\nSextants became standard equipment for celestial navigation at sea. They gave latitude directly from the Sun or stars, and when paired with an accurate marine chronometer, which John Harrison's work made practical by the 1760s, they also supported longitude calculations. The lunar distance method, promoted by Nevil Maskelyne and published in the Nautical Almanac from 1767, relied on the sextant to measure angles between the Moon and other bodies.\n\nIn the twentieth century, bubble sextants made celestial fixes possible in aircraft, and the instrument was central to air and naval navigation during the Second World War. Satellite positioning later displaced it for routine navigation, but the sextant remains part of maritime training and a symbol of the age of exploration.\n\nWORKER_TOKEN=29537106","usage":{"total_tokens":6180,"tool_uses":1,"duration_ms":6706},"uuid":"b912e3a6-c71c-4cfc-af0c-5bbeef058a0e","session_id":"f5fd90b6-eb8d-4c51-9b35-ab8874aa9f05"}
